cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tracex in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Tracex: AST-aware hybrid code search with explainable rank fusion"
abstract: >-
  Tracex retrieves source code by combining scope-preserving tree-sitter AST chunks
  with three retrieval signals (sub-token BM25, dense code embeddings and a static
  call graph), fused by weighted Reciprocal Rank Fusion and reranked by a
  cross-encoder. On a hand-labelled benchmark of 37 queries, the cross-validated
  pipeline reaches NDCG@5 = 0.784, significantly above BM25 (paired randomization
  test, Holm-adjusted p = 0.002).
type: software
